The interactive CQL playground at web/wasm-demo/ embeds a Python wheel served to Pyodide. After any Python source change or version bump, update the WASM demo: Why step 4 matters: The website's static/wasm-app/ is a pre-built snapshot served by Docusaurus. It is NOT auto-updated when web/wasm-demo/ is rebuilt. Skipping step 4 causes the standalone demo to work while the website CQL playground fails with a Pyodide error. Why duckdb is excluded from Pyodide: duckdb has no pure Python wheel on PyPI. The Pyodide worker uses deps=False and manually installs only the required pure-Python dependencies. Do not add native C extension packages as hard imports in fhir4ds.cql or any module imported by the WASM worker. See AGENTS.md and web/wasm-demo/AGENTS.md for full details.
